The relationship between fact and dimension tables is typically a one-to-many relationship, where one record in a dimension table can relate to multiple records in a fact table.
The "one" side is always a dimension table while the "many" side is always a fact table.
A measure is a fact table column that stores values to be summarized,like SUM, MIN, MAX, AVERAGE.
